# Copy this file to `.env.test` (gitignored) and fill in the URL of a
# DISPOSABLE test database. The API test suite refuses to run without it,
# so a test run can never touch the production database.
#
#   cp apps/api/.env.test.example apps/api/.env.test
#
# The guard refuses to start if TEST_DATABASE_URL points at the same
# database as DATABASE_URL in apps/api/.env (or the shell), and it pins
# DATABASE_URL to this value for the whole run, so the code under test
# cannot reach production either.
#
# Requirements for the database:
#   - PostgreSQL 14+ (the schema uses Prisma with a `postgresql` provider)
#   - the app schema applied:  npx prisma migrate deploy
#     (run from apps/api, with DATABASE_URL pointing at this database)
#
# A Neon branch is ideal - it gets its own endpoint, so the guard sees a
# different host than production and cannot be confused with it.
#
# Append these connection parameters:
#   connect_timeout=30  Neon suspends a branch when it goes idle, and waking
#                       it can take longer than Prisma's 5s default connect
#                       timeout - without the extra room the suite fails with
#                       "Can't reach database server" on a cold start.
#   pool_timeout=60     Wait for a connection from the pool instead of giving
#                       up at Prisma's 10s default.
#   connection_limit=5  Prisma's default pool is (CPU cores x 2) + 1, so on a
#                       big machine it asks for 49 connections PER client -
#                       more than a free Neon branch can serve. The suite
#                       then dies with "Timed out fetching a new connection
#                       from the connection pool". 5 is plenty: the tests
#                       run serially.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=
